There are currently in existence certain rules and regulations adopted by the Early County Board of Health with the purpose of preserving the public health, safety and welfare of the citizens of Early County, Georgia. This ordinance specifically incorporates by reference the provision of the following rules and regulations which are in force at the time of the adoption of this ordinance:
A. Rules and Regulations pertaining to Rabies Control (adopted by the Department of Public Health and the Early County Board of Health, and being Chapter 511-2-7 and Rule II—Rabies Control Ordinance, as subsequently amended and updated) and policies of the Early County Board of Health pertaining to Rabies Control;
B. Rules and Regulations pertaining to Food Service (adopted by the Department of Public Health and the Early County Board of Health, and being Chapter 511-6-1, as subsequently amended and updated) and policies of the Early County Board of Health pertaining to Food Service;
C. Rules and Regulations pertaining to Tourist Accommodations (adopted by the Department of Public Health and the Early County Board of Health, and being Chapter 511-6-2, as subsequently amended and updated) and policies of the Early County Board of Health pertaining to Tourist Accommodations;
D. Rules and Regulations for On-Site Sewage Management Systems (adopted by the Department of Public Health and the Early County Board of Health, and being Chapter 511-3-1 and Rule III—Addendum to On-site Sewage Management Systems and Subdivisions - Rules and Regulations, DPH Chapter 511-3-1, and On-site Water Supplies Rules and Regulations, as subsequently amended and updated) and policies of the Early County Board of Health pertaining to On-Site Sewage Management Systems;
E. Rules and Regulations for Portable Sanitation Contractors (adopted by the Department of Public Health and the Early County Board of Health, and being Chapter 511-3-6, and as subsequently amended and updated) and policies of the Early County Board of Health pertaining to Portable Sanitation Contractors;
F. Rules and Regulations pertaining to Drinking Water Supply (adopted by the Department of Public Health and the Early County Board of Health, and being Chapter 511-3-3, Rule III—Addendum to On-site Sewage Management Systems and Subdivisions - Rules and Regulations, DPH Chapter 511-3-1, and On-site Water Supplies Rules and Regulations, as subsequently amended and updated) and policies of the Early County Board of Health pertaining to Drinking Water Supply;
G. Rules and Regulations pertaining to Solid Waste (adopted by the Department of Public Health and the Early County Board of Health, and being Chapter 511-3-4, as subsequently amended and updated) and policies of the Early County Board of Health pertaining to Solid Waste;
H. Rules and Regulations pertaining to Public Swimming Pools, Spas and Recreational Water Parks (adopted by the Department of Public Health and the Early County Board of Health, and being Chapter 511-3-5, as subsequently amended and updated) and policies of the Early County Board of Health pertaining to Public Swimming Pools, Spas and Recreational Water Parks;
I. Rules and Regulations pertaining to Body Art (adopted by the Department of Public Health and the Early County Board of Health, and being Rules and Regulations of Early County Body Art Studios and Tattoo/Body Piercing Artists, as subsequently amended and updated) and policies of the Early County Board of Health pertaining to Body Art.
